+15. Acceptance criteria
+
+A release is not done because the dashboard renders.
+
+1. Every opportunity has source provenance and original URL.
+2. Freelance project and remote role types are visually distinct.
+3. Missing budget/rating/client spend remains unknown.
+4. No fake/sample record appears in production discovery.
+5. Re-running a provider sync creates no duplicate records.
+6. Provider failure is shown as failure, not zero opportunities.
+7. Closed/unknown/open are not conflated.
+8. Source attribution and apply URL rules are obeyed.
+9. Manual URL intake works without marketplace API credentials.
+10. Every score has explanation and confidence.
+11. Portfolio examples are user-confirmed.
+12. Proposal claims are evidence-linked.
+13. No automatic submission or external message occurs.
+14. Application status changes are auditable.
+15. UI data survives API/worker restarts.
+16. App remains operational when the user’s PC is off.
+17. Auth and owner authorization protect all private data.
+18. SSRF test suite blocks internal/private destinations.
+19. CI runs unit, integration and E2E tests.
